  ```
- **Logic**: form.js
  - When clicking the field button, call `showFieldInput(field, btn)` to display the input box for that field in the floating box.
    ```js
    function showFieldInput(field, btn) {
      // ...omitting positioning and styles...
      floatBox.innerHTML = `
        <button class="close-btn" onclick="hideFieldInput()">×</button>
        <label>${field}</label>
        <textarea id="floatInput" style="resize:vertical;">${allFieldData[field] || ''}</textarea>
      `;
      // ...omitting positioning...
      const input = document.getElementById('floatInput');
      input.focus();
      input.oninput = function() {
        allFieldData[field] = input.value;
        btn.classList.toggle('filled', !!input.value.trim());
      };
    }
    ```
  - Clicking other areas of the page or the close button calls `hideFieldInput()` to hide the floating box.

## 4. Front and Back Side Switching

- **Location**: form.html
  ```html
  <button type="button" class="side-btn" id="frontBtn">Front Preview</button>
  <button type="button" class="side-btn" id="backBtn">Back Preview</button>
  ```
- **Logic**: form.js
